{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "weno_js_nonlinear_weight",
    "description": "Pointwise classical (Jiang-Shu 1996) unnormalised WENO weight alpha = gamma/(beta + eps)^2 of one candidate stencil, from its linear weight gamma and its smoothness indicator beta, with eps = 1e-6 and power 2 -- the w1t/w2t of fire_behavior's Select_weno3 (TOL = 1e-6, on the field's own value scale; not dimensionally scaled). A face reconstruction normalises these over its candidates, sum_k alpha_k p_k / sum_k alpha_k, so the one spelling here is what both the numerator and the denominator of stencils/weno3_js_face_recon read, and eps or the power cannot drift between them. NOT the WENO-Z weight of grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/stencils/weno3_recon. Match-less helper.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:stencil",
      "family:finite_difference",
      "grid:cartesian_uniform_2d",
      "op:reconstruct",
      "order:3"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Jiang, G.-S., & Shu, C.-W. (1996). Efficient implementation of weighted ENO schemes. Journal of Computational Physics, 126(1), 202-228. The classical smoothness indicators beta_k and nonlinear weights w_k = gamma_k/(beta_k + eps)^2.",
        "doi": "10.1006/jcph.1996.0130"
      },
      {
        "citation": "NCAR Community Fire Behavior Model (fire_behavior), develop @ eb77580, physics/level_set_mod.F90: Calc_tend_ls (case 8), Select_eno, Select_weno3, Select_4th, Extrapol_var_at_bdys. The transcribed reference implementation."
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_template_imports": [],
  "expression_templates": {
    "weno_js_nonlinear_weight": {
      "params": [
        "gamma",
        "beta"
      ],
      "body": {
        "op": "/",
        "args": [
          "gamma",
          {
            "op": "^",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "+",
                "args": [
                  "beta",
                  1e-06
                ]
              },
              2
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
